# std/mem/arena/test_arena — the arena a `cf test` case runs in (testing.md §3). Structurally it IS a
# growing arena — bump allocation, elastic overflow, the standard duplex node — so it borrows
# growing_arena's whole machinery verbatim: `of__te` carves the same `el` node, the case body reserves
# through the `el` hooks (materialize folds a te body to el), and `destroy` is the same survivor
# rewind. The case's verdict is reported by an explicit call in the runner the compiler synthesizes,
# not by this geometry's teardown, so `test_arena` and `growing_arena` are behaviorally the same today;
# the name marks the role, and leaves room for a reporting teardown later.
#
# The user never names this module: `std::test::case!` opens it. A shipped binary never takes the test
# route, so it costs the artifact nothing. The surface is two tokens — `of` and `destroy` — and the
# compiler supplies both at the call site.
import std::mem::arena::growing_arena

# `test_arena.of(n)` — the constructor SURFACE: a bodyless intrinsic `case!` opens with the case's
# arena size. Lowered exactly as `growing_arena::of` (a carve from the ambient node), the node
# published so children claim through the shared elastic reserve.
pub intrinsic of = (Uarch n): Uarch

# `test_arena::destroy(b)` — the teardown: dissolve the case's carved arena `b` back into its parent by
# a survivor rewind to its base (the carve mark, reached via the parent link at `b+16`). User-placed by
# `case!`'s lowering (`|> defer destroy`); the compiler supplies the behavior at the call site.
pub intrinsic destroy = (Uarch node): ()
